{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Scope\n\nDraft stacked Spatial Library refit for Assets, Environments, Scenes, Effects and Compositions. It keeps one left rail, source-grounded previews, search/filter/sort/grid/list controls, bounded paging, owned Scene actions, contextual insertion and surface-aware physical drag placement. SC-01 owns Environment/Scene lifecycle, SC-02 owns model/effect definitions, and SC-07A owns Community publication.\n\n## Source-bound local evidence on this PR\n\n- The latest Library journey passed 1/1 on product source `bbf2a53aff43a69b0a12f5e712c723cd957d7593` (tree `a3291e71656689367314baa6f190ec052891c782`), including archive confirmation. Receipt and screenshots: `Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00c/20261015-archive-pass/`.\n- A prior `6d2dbf278d18cbc39b218326a466549ed43d91dd` source passed 4/4 Library and owner journeys: real thumbnails, click/Effect drag, Undo/Redo, invalid placement feedback, positive pointer-positioned floor drop and selection, Environment/Scene traversal, owner actions, composition reuse, keyboard browse and 48-card paging. Its receipt and screenshots remain in `evidence/sc-00c/20261015-final/`.\n- The workstation run on `2c943256361fa922f7dc964be9a2649c65142a16` passed 2/2 journeys across six widths and three layouts. Older failed attempts remain preserved. These results apply to their exact local sources only.\n\n## Integration branch and current limits\n\nThe separately owned `codex/parallax-sc-00c-env-projection` branch is pushed at `93ca4fb079246ac71a82ba8f602b287c432599b8`. Its `12a5919d` source passed an authenticated SC-00 Environment/Library bridge journey 1/1, and its `e0fea9f7` source passed a 390 px Library compactness journey 1/1. The phone screenshot shows initial categories, search and the first two asset cards with secondary filters collapsed; expanded controls remain accessible. Evidence: `Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00c/20261015-bridge-pass/` and `.../20261015-phone-pass/`.\n\nThe D branch also includes SC-01's typed legacy catalog source `6be365f2`, SC-00C's working-over-release projection `edd4ed73`, and a narrow Library detail-copy correction at `59bb1506`. The authenticated browser journey on that copy source passed 1/1 with valid source binding and a visually inspected screenshot: current working name, description and organization metadata remain distinct from an immutable release, while the detail copy identifies a read-only fixture preview, separate working document and pinned immutable versions. Its exact-source evidence is `Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00c/20261015-legacy-working-copy-pass/`. The earlier pass with a copy finding is preserved in `.../20261015-legacy-working-first-pass/`. These D-branch commits are **not in this PR head** and do not establish combined-source acceptance.\n\nThe D branch's bounded Library action source `0e7fabdb` passed a further authenticated 1/1 action-visibility journey. It exposes owned typed legacy working Edit, Save, Archive/Restore and associated Scenes; built-ins can enter an owned-copy flow; immutable release review goes through an optional SC-01 Manager callback. It does not present legacy Save As/version dialogs or a fabricated direct-Use/current pin. Evidence: `Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00c/20261015-legacy-actions-pass/`. This local run did not exercise the combined SC-01 Manager host callbacks.\n\nThe SC-00 owner is integrating the Environment/Scene bridge and reviewed SC-02 source in a separate owned checkout. The Library component exposes a saved-composition callback and pointer drag contract, but the combined host/canvas behavior requires exact-candidate browser proof. SC-01 Manager/writer mount, the global phone header, combined SC-02 viewport layout, installed-Community composition lineage, independent combined review and protected qualification remain separate work. The standalone PR source is therefore draft and not independently mergeable. Main remains protected; Crossdeck's experience-design gate has not been bypassed. Local browser proof is neither physical-device nor owner acceptance.\n\n## Review focus\n\nReview the five-category information architecture, private/Chronicle/Community language, Environment working and immutable-version preservation, keyboard and phone layout, owner actions, and pointer placement. Use exact source IDs for every receipt.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:18:37Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:18:37Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Add reusable Environment revisions and independent Scene management","oid":"b517648f0bd4a734056148f51b953ac70ad2f410"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:34:17Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:34:17Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Isolate Environment editing and preserve Scene save and preview state","oid":"ce32674cc7147ca46ed18628255bc0529423a337"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:43:40Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:43:40Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Preserve built-in Environment digests through production serialization","oid":"4d022dcf4e4688b033577e43593e400452c5e991"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:47:37Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T03:47:37Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"feat(parallax): prepare SC-02 assets and spatial effects candidate","oid":"975016c887416a14e1a1d817c4fcc90f90165aee"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T03:54:02Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"com